FIELDS = ['name','lab','levels','status','kind','focus','timing','eligibility','materials','action','source']
programs = [dict(zip(FIELDS,row),id=f'pathway-{i:02d}',reviewed='2026-11-09') for i,row in enumerate(DATA,1)]
assert len(programs)==30
(ROOT/'data').mkdir(exist_ok=True)
(ROOT/'data'/'opportunities.json').write_text(json.dumps(programs,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False),encoding='utf-8')
(DOCS/'downloads').mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
with (DOCS/'downloads'/'opportunities.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:
    writer=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=list(programs[0]));writer.writeheader();writer.writerows(programs)
with (DOCS/'downloads'/'application-tracker.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:
    writer=csv.writer(f);writer.writerow(['Program','Lab','Official URL','Job ID','Eligibility confirmed','Deadline and timezone','Mentor','Contact date','Follow-up date','Recommenders','Letters received','Application status','Interview date','Decision','Next action','Next action date']);writer.writerow(['Example: replace this row','','','','','','','','','','','','','','',''])
labels={'us-lpr':'U.S. citizen / permanent resident','us':'U.S. citizen','international':'International pathway · conditions apply','verify':'Confirm with program'}
intro='''---
hide:
  - toc
---
# Find your laboratory pathway

30 curated opportunities and research routes across the national laboratory system. Start with academic level, then check eligibility and research fit. **These are editorial selections, not a ranking or a claim that 30 vacancies are open.** Fellowships and faculty collaborations are labeled separately.

<div class="note">Reviewed November 9, 2026. “International pathway” means the source describes access for some noncitizens or applicants authorized to work in the U.S.; it does not guarantee sponsorship or site access. “Confirm with program” means the overview does not resolve citizenship eligibility. Permanent residents are noncitizens but have a separate filter category.</div>

<div class="filter-panel">
<div class="filters">
<label>Research, lab or keyword<input id="op-search" type="search" placeholder="Try Sandia, computing, energy…"></label>
<label>Academic level<select id="op-level"><option value="">All academic levels</option><option value="community">Community college</option><option value="undergraduate">Undergraduate</option><option value="graduate">Graduate</option><option value="recent">Recent graduate</option><option value="faculty">Faculty</option></select></label>
<label>Eligibility category<select id="op-status"><option value="">All categories</option><option value="us-lpr">U.S. citizen / permanent resident</option><option value="us">U.S. citizen</option><option value="international">International pathway</option><option value="verify">Confirm with program</option></select></label>
</div>
<div class="filter-footer"><span id="result-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">30 pathways</span><label><input id="saved-only" type="checkbox"> My saved pathways</label><button id="reset-filters" type="button">Reset filters</button><a href="../downloads/opportunities.csv" download>Download all 30 · CSV ↓</a></div>
</div>
<p class="fine">Filters identify routes to investigate, not a complete eligibility determination. U.S. citizens may also qualify for international pathways or programs marked “confirm.” Save buttons use this browser’s local storage; no account or server submission is involved.</p>
<p id="no-results" class="empty-state" hidden>No pathways match these filters. Try another academic level or reset the filters.</p>
<div class="opportunity-grid">
'''
cards=[]
e=html.escape
for i,p in enumerate(programs,1):
    cards.append(f'''<article class="opportunity" id="{p['id']}" data-level="{p['levels']}" data-status="{p['status']}">
<div class="meta">{i:02d} / {e(p['lab'])}</div><h2>{e(p['name'])}</h2>
<div><span class="badge">{e(p['kind'])}</span><span class="badge variable">{labels[p['status']]}</span></div>
<p><strong>Research fit:</strong> {e(p['focus'])}</p><p><strong>Level:</strong> {e(p['levels'].replace(' ', ' · '))}</p><p><strong>Timing:</strong> {e(p['timing'])}</p>
<details><summary>Eligibility, materials &amp; next step</summary><p><strong>Eligibility:</strong> {e(p['eligibility'])}</p><p><strong>Prepare:</strong> {e(p['materials'])}</p><p><strong>Next step:</strong> {e(p['action'])}</p><p>Source reviewed {p['reviewed']}. Confirm deadline, compensation and available projects on the current official page.</p></details>
<div class="actions"><a href="{e(p['source'])}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official program ↗</a><button type="button" class="save-button" data-id="{p['id']}" aria-label="Save {e(p['name'])}" aria-pressed="false">Save pathway</button></div></article>''')
(DOCS/'opportunities.md').write_text(intro+'\n'.join(cards)+'\n</div>\n',encoding='utf-8')
register='''# Sources & editorial upkeep

This independent guide is for planning. Official program pages, current job postings and program offices determine requirements and selections. It is not affiliated with DOE or any laboratory. The guides contain editorial preparation advice; suggested outreach timing and document organization are not universal program requirements.

## What was reviewed

The directory was researched on **November 9, 2026** using the following official laboratory and DOE sources. Some catalog pages describe a program without publishing a current application window. A review date is not a guarantee that applications are open. Each record separates known eligibility from details to confirm.

“Top 30” is interpreted as a curated starting set across levels, topics and eligibility routes, not a measured quality ranking. We avoid counting the same SULI program once for every host. Faculty-led, fellowship and student-employment routes are included because they offer distinct ways to conduct laboratory research.

| Pathway | Official source | Review date |
| --- | --- | --- |
'''
for p in programs: register+=f"| {p['name']} | [Program source]({p['source']}) | {p['reviewed']} |\n"
register+='''
## Additional application references

- [SULI application instructions](https://science.osti.gov/wdts/suli/How-to-Apply) — application documents and online recommendations.
- [SULI FAQs](https://science.osti.gov/wdts/suli/Frequently-Asked-Questions) — current term-specific questions and dates.
- [CCI application instructions](https://science.osti.gov/wdts/cci/How-to-Apply/) — transcript and recommendation submission.
- [SCGSR FAQs](https://science.osti.gov/wdts/scgsr/Frequently-Asked-Questions) — thesis collaboration, application and participation conditions.
- [Sandia internship requirements](https://www.sandia.gov/careers/careers/students-and-postdocs/internships-co-ops/) — academic and application requirements.
- [LLNL student hiring overview](https://www.llnl.gov/join-our-team/careers/student-internship-veteran-programs) — hiring and international-student considerations.
- [Fermilab internship FAQs](https://internships.fnal.gov/faqs/) — international students and program-specific eligibility.

## Maintain this guide

1. Assign a faculty owner and student ambassador in each participating department; record real contacts locally before announcing office hours.
2. During recruitment, review program links and deadlines monthly and again two weeks before a promoted deadline. Review the full directory each semester.
3. Edit `build_content.py` for directory records, regenerate with `python build_content.py`, then run `mkdocs build --strict`. The JSON dataset and CSV download are generated from the same records.
4. Record the reviewed date, URL, academic level, citizenship, authorization, deadline with timezone, funding and current contact. Do not infer citizenship from a lab name.
5. If a source is unclear, retain “confirm with program.” If a program is suspended, mark it accordingly or replace the record, and explain the change in the repository history.
6. Ask students for opt-in, anonymized feedback about confusing instructions. Program offices handle official eligibility questions; international offices handle individual authorization questions.

**Current limits:** most deadlines and compensation are deliberately linked to the current announcement because they vary by term or position. The directory does not automatically refresh and the browser shortlist does not sync between devices. No department contact roster has been supplied yet.
'''
(DOCS/'sources.md').write_text(register,encoding='utf-8')
print(f'Generated {len(programs)} pathways, source register, JSON and CSV downloads.')
